## Filter Implementation

**Source location:** `source/src/runtime/types.ts:2918-2928`

### FilterIter Class

```typescript
export class FilterIter {
  constructor(public f: any, public it: any) {}
  $next(): any {
    for (;;) {
      const value = this.it.$next();
      if (value === DONE) return DONE;
      if (this.f === null ? O.truth(value) : O.truth(callObj(this.f, [value]))) return value;
    }
  }
}
```

### Answers to Your Questions

1. **Truth-testing when predicate is None vs callable:**
   - **When `predicate is None`**: truth-tests the **source item itself** (`O.truth(value)`)
   - **When predicate is callable**: truth-tests the **predicate's return value** (`O.truth(callObj(this.f, [value]))`)

2. **Returned value:**
   - The returned value is **the source item** (`return value`), not the predicate result—regardless of which branch executes

3. **Source exhaustion:**
   - When the source iterator is exhausted (returns `DONE`), the filter iterator immediately returns `DONE`, terminating iteration

The key line encodes this: `if (this.f === null ? O.truth(value) : O.truth(callObj(this.f, [value]))) return value;`
